1. Why Do We Need Spark?

Imagine you have a CSV file of 5 TB.

A normal Python program would

Read File
↓

Store in RAM
↓

Process
↓

Write Output

Problems:

Single CPU
Limited RAM
Very slow
Cannot process TBs of data efficiently

Now imagine we have 10 machines.

Instead of one machine processing the file,

Machine 1 → 500 GB

Machine 2 → 500 GB

Machine 3 → 500 GB

...

Machine 10 → 500 GB

Now every machine works simultaneously.

This is called

Distributed Computing

Spark is a distributed computing engine.


2. What is Apache Spark?

Definition (Interview):

Apache Spark is an open-source distributed data processing engine designed for high-speed large-scale data processing using in-memory computation.

Keywords

Distributed
Parallel
In-memory
Fault Tolerant
Fast

